{"Django querysets do not support negative indexing - queryset[negative_start:stop] raises AssertionError. The branch handling cursor.offset < 0 with enable_advanced_features=True will always raise AssertionError at runtime.": 0.9398345351219177, "organization_context.member can be None when the requesting user is not a member of the organization (e.g., staff user without superuser status), causing AttributeError when accessing .has_global_access on None. Needs a guard check.": 0.7798359394073486, "OptimizedCursorPaginator.get_item_key() applies math.floor/math.ceil directly to raw attribute values, but when used with datetime objects (e.g., order_by=\"-datetime\" in audit logs), it raises TypeError because datetime objects are not real numbers. Needs conversion to float millisecond timestamp like DateTimePaginator.get_item_key() does.": 0.9940415024757385, "value_from_cursor() returns raw cursor value (integer timestamp) instead of converting it back to a datetime, causing incorrect results or database errors when build_queryset() uses this value to filter datetime columns against raw integers. Should convert like DateTimePaginator.value_from_cursor() does.": 0.9846131801605225}